 "evidence_class": "SYNTHETIC_FAKEVENUE_WINDOWS_WORKSTATION",
 "finding": "Kept on purpose: the first 1,000-account run used a 1.5 s drill TTL. A maintenance round took ~2 s on this loaded workstation, so leases lapsed mid-round: the fence refused those steps (no mutation by a worker that no longer owned the account) and the accounts moved to other workers, which recovered them first. SQLite: 1,334 claims reported for 1,000 accounts in one round (rebalance moves); PostgreSQL: 517 of 1,000 maintained in that round. Safe, but churn: the lease TTL must exceed the round duration with margin. Production TTL is 60 s. The committed scale_1000_accounts.json uses a 5 s drill TTL. This file predates the fence_refused_lease_lapsed counter, so the lapse shows as the gap between owned / accounts_maintained and the account count.",
